# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/prefill-3 window (the masked tail pass of a prompt as a trace replay; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/prefill-3 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the
# order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-pf3-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (sed -i 's/tp4-pf3-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file
# the image carries needs a new B0 build and a NEW tag in every template (a rebuild under an existing tag keeps the old image). This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# C2_MODEL_REPO / C2_MODEL_REVISION (qwen_c2_checkpoint.py): a smoke job that carries them serves the Swift checkpoint (what production serves) from its own converted-weight directory; the keys are the same
# in every smoke job of this pack, so each pair differs by the profile alone. The prefix steps (AP1, R1, R2) do not forward the selection into their container and serve the base checkpoint: a tail pass
# replays the same traces on either.
# A1 (EXACTNESS of the traced tail, buckets 128 and 1,024, STOP): c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-pf3-s5-audit, the ship-5 audited twin without W3 WC (every
# audit of the candidate) with QWEN_FAST_PREFILL_TAIL_TRACE=1, the buckets 128,1024 and QWEN_FAST_PREFILL_TAIL_TRACE_AUDIT=1, on Swift. The first 8 traced tails, every 24th
# after and the first two of each bucket run the STOCK pass beside the replay (the scratch restored between them) and require every GDN recurrent state, conv carry and conv
# window, every real row of the output and every drafter tap row byte equal; the stock result is what the request is served. Tests: warmup; coding (one user); parked_turns
# (eight seats, forty closed-loop turns of 4k to 24k tokens: forty tail passes of every bucket, beside seven decoding seats); prefill_ladder_solo (one request at a time at
# about 4k, 32k, 128k and 254k tokens: four tail passes); prefill_few_decoders (one decoding seat beside a 120k-token arrival and two beside a 254k one); concurrent8_steady
# (eight users, then the octo rounds, which the lever never touches); agent_turns (six sessions of 64k to 200k tokens of coding context, twelve returning turns each: about
# seventy returning-turn tail passes of every bucket at the production context sizes). READ: c2_smoke_check clean; "[PINDIAG] prefill tail trace audit n=<k> exact=True
# bucket=.. valid=.. layers=48 taps=5" for every audited tail (a bucket-128 and a bucket-1,024 line at least twice each), NO "audit mismatch" (it raises and names the first
# state: "layer <i> recurrent state" is claim C1 false, "layer <i> conv window" is C2 false, "tap layer <i> rows" is the tap hand-off, "the output rows" is the attention or
# K/V path), NO "fell back"; the engaged line says uncovered=0. Two buckets and not four because the audited stack leaves the trace region 114.8 MB free after the first
# packed round. ANY failure is NO-GO for the lever and halts the window. the lines in the container log: "[PINDIAG] lever N route installed: ... tailtrace=traced audit"
# once; on the arms "[PINDIAG] prefill tail trace engaged buckets=.. traces=<n> sink=<id> taps=5,19,33,47,61 arena_mb=<mb> arena_address=.. freed=<k> uncovered=0
# capture_ms=.." once and one "[PF3] tail mode=traced bucket=.. valid=.. start=.. ms=.. stage_ms=.. replay_ms=.." per traced tail pass; on the control one "[PF3] tail
# mode=eager bucket=.. valid=.. start=.. ms=.." per tail pass below the 2,048-row bucket and no "engaged" line; no "fell back" line, no "[PF3] tail skip" line that the
# control would not also take (a skip is a call that ran the stock pass: vision, an untraced bucket, another page-table width, another tap set) and no program growth after
# the warm anywhere MEMORY READ (the ledger is on in these profiles): "[MEMLEDGER] phase=P7 ... trace_used=.." per chip after the attach is the trace region the lever's
# traces took (against the control's P7 line: python3 -B scripts/ci/pf3_report.py --control <control log> --arm <this log>, or --headroom <log> for the fit of N traces),
# and the P7 DRAM line is what the arena holds (the arena is 320 MB a chip at its default; the admission need of a prompt of 2,048 tokens or more is unchanged, so a "dram
# admission hold" that the control did not draw is the arena's) CHECKPOINT READ (the workflow passes c2_smoke_check.py --expect-checkpoint): the container log holds
# "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b@b4c84d42903a key=... weight_cache=.../weights-ckpt/<key> base_cache=... (the base cache is not read or written)" once,
# a "weight cache ...: found" line (the cache the Swift window built; this pack never builds it) and the worker's "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint bound ..." line; the models answer
# names ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b. RUN WITH THE CI PAUSED. Duration (estimate): 100 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-pf3-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-pf3-s5-audit
C2_MODEL_REPO=ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b
C2_MODEL_REVISION=b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,parked_turns,prefill_ladder_solo,concurrent8_steady,agent_turns
C2_TELEMETRY=1
C2_BOX_MINUTES=165
